{"title":"Career Roadmap — Videographer","role":"Videographer","summary":"Role overview:\nA Videographer plans, captures and produces video content for films, documentaries, corporate communications, advertising, social media, events, education, news, weddings and digital platforms. The role combines camera operation, lighting, composition, sound, storytelling, editing and production coordination.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Photography / Sound Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Camera portfolio + production internship"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Professional videography + editing"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Cinematography/production leadership"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Creative direction + technology + business"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Photography / Sound Engineering","Video Production Internship","Camera/Production Assistant","Videographer","Senior Videographer / Cinematographer","Director of Photography / Video Production Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is a strong alignment, particularly because the programme combines visual production with technical audio knowledge."},{"type":"note","label":"Timeline assumption","text":"The roadmap assumes the student starts UG in 2026. B.Sc duration may be 3 or 4 years depending on the university/programme."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Photography + visual fundamentals"},{"text":"College + practical shooting"},{"text":"Photo portfolio"},{"text":"Visual foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Camera + composition"},{"text":"Camera practice"},{"text":"10–15 short videos"},{"text":"Camera skills"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Lighting + sound"},{"text":"Studio/field practice"},{"text":"Interview + controlled-light shoot"},{"text":"Production quality"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Video editing"},{"text":"Premiere Pro/DaVinci Resolve"},{"text":"3 edited projects"},{"text":"Post-production"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Storytelling + cinematography"},{"text":"Short films/documentaries"},{"text":"2–3 narrative projects"},{"text":"Creative skill"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Production internship"},{"text":"Production house/media company"},{"text":"Internship portfolio"},{"text":"Industry readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Advanced production"},{"text":"Cinematography + colour"},{"text":"Short film/documentary"},{"text":"Professional capability"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Portfolio + freelancing"},{"text":"Real client work"},{"text":"Showreel + professional portfolio"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core technical stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Camera fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exposure"},{"text":"Aperture"},{"text":"Shutter speed"},{"text":"ISO"},{"text":"White balance"},{"text":"Frame rates"},{"text":"Resolution"},{"text":"Bit depth"},{"text":"Codecs"},{"text":"Picture profiles"},{"text":"Log footage"},{"text":"Dynamic range"},{"text":"Lens selection"},{"text":"Focal length"},{"text":"Depth of field"},{"text":"Focus"},{"text":"Manual exposure"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the difference between:"},{"type":"h","text":"24 fps → cinematic motion"},{"type":"h","text":"25/30 fps → standard video production"},{"type":"h","text":"50/60 fps → slow-motion possibilities"},{"type":"p","text":"Actual production settings should depend on the project, camera and delivery platform."}]},{"heading":"Composition","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rule of thirds"},{"text":"Leading lines"},{"text":"Symmetry"},{"text":"Framing"},{"text":"Negative space"},{"text":"Depth"},{"text":"Foreground/background"},{"text":"Headroom"},{"text":"Look room"},{"text":"Visual balance"},{"text":"Camera perspective"},{"text":"Shot continuity"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to deliberately choose:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Wide shot","Medium shot","Close-up","Detail shot"]},{"type":"p","text":"rather than recording everything from a single angle."}]},{"heading":"Cinematography","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Shot sizes"},{"text":"Camera angles"},{"text":"Camera movement"},{"text":"Dolly"},{"text":"Pan"},{"text":"Tilt"},{"text":"Tracking"},{"text":"Handheld"},{"text":"Gimbal"},{"text":"Crane/jib"},{"text":"Static composition"},{"text":"Lens language"},{"text":"Visual continuity"},{"text":"Motivated camera movement"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to decide why the camera should move, not simply how to make it move."}]},{"heading":"Lighting","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Three-point lighting"},{"text":"Key light"},{"text":"Fill light"},{"text":"Back/rim light"},{"text":"Hard vs soft light"},{"text":"Natural light"},{"text":"Practical lights"},{"text":"LED panels"},{"text":"Fresnel lights"},{"text":"Diffusion"},{"text":"Reflectors"},{"text":"Flags"},{"text":"Negative fill"},{"text":"Colour temperature"},{"text":"Mixed lighting"},{"text":"Low-key/high-key lighting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Projects should include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview lighting"},{"text":"Product lighting"},{"text":"Portrait lighting"},{"text":"Indoor scene"},{"text":"Outdoor scene"},{"text":"Night scene"}]}]},{"heading":"Audio and sound","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Because the programme includes Sound Engineering, audio can become a major competitive advantage."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microphone types"},{"text":"Lavalier microphones"},{"text":"Shotgun microphones"},{"text":"Dynamic microphones"},{"text":"Condenser microphones"},{"text":"Audio interfaces"},{"text":"Recorders"},{"text":"Gain staging"},{"text":"Clipping"},{"text":"Noise floor"},{"text":"Signal-to-noise ratio"},{"text":"Room acoustics"},{"text":"Boom operation"},{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Sync sound"},{"text":"Audio cleanup"},{"text":"Dialogue editing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"p","text":"Good video + bad audio = poor production quality."}]},{"heading":"Video editing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop professional editing skills in at least one major platform:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DaVinci Resolve"},{"text":"Adobe Premiere Pro"},{"text":"Final Cut Pro"}]},{"type":"p","text":"DaVinci Resolve","url":"https://www.blackmagicdesign.com/products/davinciresolve"},{"type":"p","text":"Adobe Premiere Pro","url":"https://www.adobe.com/products/premiere.html"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Timeline editing"},{"text":"Cutting"},{"text":"Trimming"},{"text":"Transitions"},{"text":"B-roll"},{"text":"J-cuts"},{"text":"L-cuts"},{"text":"Multicam editing"},{"text":"Audio mixing"},{"text":"Titles"},{"text":"Subtitles"},{"text":"Motion graphics basics"},{"text":"Proxy workflows"},{"text":"Export settings"}]}]},{"heading":"Colour correction and grading","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the difference between:"},{"type":"h","text":"Colour correction → technically balancing footage"},{"type":"p","text":"and"},{"type":"p","text":"Colour grading → creating a deliberate visual style."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exposure"},{"text":"Contrast"},{"text":"White balance"},{"text":"Skin tones"},{"text":"Saturation"},{"text":"Curves"},{"text":"LUTs"},{"text":"Scopes"},{"text":"Waveform"},{"text":"Vectorscope"},{"text":"Colour management"},{"text":"Log-to-display workflows"}]}]},{"heading":"Storytelling","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Technical camera skills alone do not make a strong videographer."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Story structure"},{"text":"Character"},{"text":"Conflict"},{"text":"Narrative progression"},{"text":"Interview technique"},{"text":"B-roll storytelling"},{"text":"Visual sequencing"},{"text":"Pacing"},{"text":"Emotional beats"},{"text":"Documentary storytelling"},{"text":"Brand storytelling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong portfolio should demonstrate that the student can tell a story, not merely produce visually attractive footage."}]},{"heading":"Production workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand the complete pipeline:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Idea","Brief","Research","Script","Shot list","Storyboard","Production plan","Location","Equipment","Shoot","Backup","Edit","Colour","Sound","Review","Export","Delivery"]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to maintain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Shot lists"},{"text":"Call sheets"},{"text":"Production schedules"},{"text":"Equipment lists"},{"text":"Location notes"},{"text":"Release/permission records"},{"text":"File naming"},{"text":"Backup systems"},{"text":"Version control"}]}]},{"heading":"Storage and data management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Professional video creates large amounts of data."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Memory-card management"},{"text":"Data transfer"},{"text":"File organisation"},{"text":"Proxy workflows"},{"text":"Local backup"},{"text":"Cloud backup"},{"text":"RAID concepts"},{"text":"Version management"},{"text":"Archiving"},{"text":"Metadata"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A simple professional principle:"},{"type":"p","text":"Never treat the camera memory card as the only copy of important footage."}]},{"heading":"AI and modern video production","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted editing"},{"text":"Automatic transcription"},{"text":"AI subtitles"},{"text":"Object tracking"},{"text":"Noise reduction"},{"text":"Generative video tools"},{"text":"AI colour workflows"},{"text":"Automated reframing"},{"text":"Content repurposing"},{"text":"AI-assisted storyboarding"},{"text":"Synthetic voice/audio workflows"},{"text":"AI content ethics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should improve production efficiency while the videographer retains responsibility for creative decisions, accuracy, consent and copyright."},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio projects"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, aim for:"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Short documentary"},{"type":"p","text":"5–10 minutes covering a real person, place or community."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Corporate video"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a professional company/profile video."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Event video"},{"type":"p","text":"Capture an event from preparation through completion."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Product video"},{"type":"p","text":"Shoot and edit a product advertisement."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Interview"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a professionally lit and recorded interview."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 6 — Short film"},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate cinematography, storytelling and sound."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 7 — Social-media campaign"},{"type":"p","text":"Create multiple short-form videos for Instagram/YouTube/other platforms."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 8 — Final-year production"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Pre-production","cinematography","sound","editing","colour","distribution"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation options"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Learn from","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":"Cinematography"},{"text":"Camera, lighting, lenses"},{"text":"Film 